# Panel dropdowns — Chakra Menu

For **enum / preset / charset** fields in the React panel (`apps/web/`), use **`PanelSelect`** (`apps/web/src/components/ui/PanelSelect.tsx`), which wraps Chakra **`Menu`** (trigger + portal list + checkmark).

## Do

- Reuse **`PanelSelect`** for charset, access mode, presets, and similar single-choice fields.
- Reference: `PanelSelect.tsx`, `LocaleSelector.tsx` (same Menu pattern).
- In **`Dialog`**, pass **`zIndex={1400}`** so the list renders above the modal.

```tsx
<PanelSelect
  value={draft.charset}
  options={charsetOptions}
  zIndex={1400}
  onChange={(charset) => patch({ charset })}
/>
```

## Do not (new code)

- Do not use **`Select.Root`** / **`Select.HiddenSelect`** in dialogs or shared form pickers — Zag’s `syncSelectElement` can throw (`selectEl.options is not iterable`).
- Do not add new **`NativeSelect`** for user-facing choice lists unless there is a strong reason.
- Do not use raw HTML `<select>`.

Legacy screens may still use `NativeSelect` or `Select` until migrated.

## Menu vs Select

| Component | Use for |
|-----------|---------|
| **`Menu`** / **`PanelSelect`** | Pick one value from a fixed list (form state) |
| **`Select`** | Only where a native hidden `<select>` is required for HTML form submit (rare) |
| **`NativeSelect`** | Legacy only; prefer `PanelSelect` when touching the file |
